Database plotting

Okay, let's talk about drawing points (airports, intersections) (and eventually, but not
now, nonpoint features like airspace boundaries, TFRs) on the chart in the UI.

  Point vectors are now available as a first-cut side artifact under <source-root>/../aerobag-artifacts/product-builds/shared/work/
  vectors-2604/output/ . The current zip is vectors_2604.zip and contains separate tiled point files by layer:
  point_tiles_airport_z9.json, point_tiles_fix_z10.json, point_tiles_nav_z9.json, point_tiles_awos_z9.json, and
  point_tiles_obstacle_z12.json, plus stats.json and a small vectors manifest. Each tile file is a simple JSON object with
  schema_version, zoom, and a tiles[] array; each tile has z/x/y and records[], and each record has id, kind, lat, lon, label, and
  style_class. Current measured maxima are airport 107, fix 128, nav 9, awos 10, obstacle 286. This is also wired into the product
  build graph, so the next successful build-product run will materialize the same vectors node in the normal shared outputs.

Let's start on the web side and get that how we want it first.
Let's start drawing intersections. Cyan solid triangle, name in all caps.

Let's draw airports. For now, a magenta circle with the airport code adjacent. Clip off the ICAO K prefix.
(but don't clip it off of a 3-letter airport code that happens to start with K!)
Now variations for types of airports:
	With control tower? It's blue.
	With fuel? It gets dashes.
	Draw the biggest runway orientation as a white bar.

